//! The `scroll-timeline` [CSS](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS)
//! [shorthand](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Guides/Cascade/Shorthand_properties)
//! property is used to define a [named scroll progress
//! timeline](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Guides/Scroll-driven_animations/Timelines#named_scroll_progress_timelines),
//! which is progressed through by scrolling a scrollable element (_scroller_) between top and bottom
//! (or left and right).
//!
//! Initial: scroll-timeline-name: none; scroll-timeline-axis: block. Inherited: no.
//! Percentages: not accepted.
//!
//! Grammar: [ <'scroll-timeline-name'> <'scroll-timeline-axis'>? ]#
//!
//! Specification: https://drafts.csswg.org/scroll-animations-1/#propdef-scroll-timeline
//!
//! Author guide:
//! https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/scroll-timeline
//!
//! Purpose and value descriptions adapted from MDN contributors (CC-BY-SA-2.5).
//!
//! Generated from @webref/css 8.7.8. Do not edit.

